871 0 obj
  << /ActualText (If I am browsing the internet today\054 I might need to get the url from browser recommendation\054 by the act of typing a few characters\056\056\056\n\nSimilarly when I am on tomorrow\031s internet\054 I will do the same thing but sometimes with the added idea of which data sink I am expecting to open up\056\056\056\n\nWhich doesn\031t mean all my activity would be in expectation of opening a data sink I want\056\056\056\n\nAll intelligence\054 search\054 social\054 backlinks will remain as it is\n\nI wouldn\031t care to change the data sink of every possible website that provides that function\n\nProbably\054 want to keep accessing intelligence\054 search\054 social\054 backlinks as it is\n\nMaybe some I expect to open a particular data sink on each different internet workspace)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 872 0 R
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

872 0 obj
  << /K [ 871 0 R ]
     /P 883 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

873 0 obj
  << /ActualText (But there would be times I would be actively organising the websites I want on a particular internet workspace\n\nThese would be times when I want to separate a project from my future activity\n\nIf I am currently starting a new project\054 I might start a new internet workspace as well\n\nThese are two events when I will be more concerned about the workspace capability the internet provides\nStarting a Project\nJust Saving my Progress\n\nWhat the conclusion I bring here is\054 we need to think about the internet as two activities and enable them both to happen for the user\nWhen they are concerned about the internet workspaces\054 that activity should be available on hand when the thought arises\nWhen they are not concerned about the internet workspaces\054 that activity should be achievable when the IE functionality just doesn\031t seem to exist\n)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 874 0 R
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

874 0 obj
  << /K [ 873 0 R ]
     /P 883 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

875 0 obj
  << /ActualText (We are not storing the data sink identifiers of an application\056\n\nA Workspace Permanent ID\ncore URL\nTemporary ID \055 This is itself distinct for each workspace\054 remains the same over months and years\054 and probably should be encrypted\056 But then CDNs\056 and reverse proxies won\031t be able to decrypt prolly\056\n\nThe picture is of a cloud with the above data\054 and just that being the entire system\056 Even though that\031s not the exact case\056 When a device sends the right credentials\054 it downloads this on the client\056\n\n\nWe are not storing device IDs \nEven though we need to deliver and receive the core URLs\nDeliver to sync devices\nReceive to stay current\nUnless explicitly wanted by the user\n\nTrusted Devices send updates\054 we can\031t know\057derive their location\056 we just check if they are trusted\056\nLikewise\054 they poll for receiving updates\056 Thus we do not need to store device IDs\054 unless user wants\056\n)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 876 0 R
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

876 0 obj
  << /K [ 875 0 R ]
     /P 883 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

877 0 obj
  << /ActualText (ChatGPT\072\nI think this is a good working assumption to carry forward\056\nCurrent design principles\072\n The Workspace Service stores only the minimum persistent information\072\n Permanent Workspace ID\n Core URL\n Temporary Workspace ID \057 Handle \050if needed\051\n Data Sink identifiers are not stored by the Workspace Service\056\n Device IDs are not stored by default\056\n Clients authenticate as trusted participants\073 the service verifies trust rather than maintaining a device registry\056\n Clients push updates and poll\057subscribe for updates\056\n Persistent device records exist only if they enable an explicit user\055facing feature \050e\056g\056 trusted devices\054 remote sign\055out\054 device management\051\056\nThe key principle is\072\nNothing should be persisted unless the protocol or a user\055visible capability requires it\056\nThis gives you a strong default until a concrete requirement forces an exception\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 878 0 R
     /Pg 861 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

